  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1245 PM MDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nNorthwest flow aloft keeping cooler conditions in place over\nIdaho today with highs remaining in the 80s in lower elevations,\nbut also spreading some wildfire smoke into the state with air\nquality advisories in effect. Upper ridge begins to build in\nfrom the west Wednesday and will start to see significant\nwarming begin tomorrow with many low elevation highs back \naround 90 once again with the upper 90s by Thursday and Friday \nand into the weekend. Very hot conditions are returning. Grids \nin the long term do have some moisture finally returning with \nvery low chances of thunderstorms Monday and Tuesday in the \nextreme southeast corner of the state but very low confidence \nin that happening. Main impact short term will be the wildfire \nsmoke air quality, then by late week and the weekend it will be \nthe extreme heat once again.",
